# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two FILES, never a
# shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is defined in run_gates.sh.
# Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_go_same_package_constvar_recall.py" "GO SAME-PACKAGE CONSTVAR RECALL GATE: PASS" "go same-package const/var recall — measured boundary + precision lock" "go same-package const/var recall: an audit (audit/extractor-recall-3) measured with the product's OWN tools (recall_measure.py co-change ground truth, lift>=2 & support>=3, shipping dampened adjacency, cutoff 8) found the DOMINANT real coupling the live engine misses on Go repos is SAME-PACKAGE symbol use through package-level const/var: logrus live recall 44.6pct with 20 no-edge SAME-DIR (= same Go package) missed pairs, cobra 45.9pct with 16 — dampening cost 0.0 pts = PURE extractor blindness (in Go every file in a directory shares one package and sees siblings' top-level symbols with NO import, and a bare value reference is not a call_expression, so there is neither an import nor a calls edge). HONEST NO (measured upstream-blocked boundary, not a guess): the only recovery is to emit an edge for a bare IDENTIFIER reference to a package-level const/var, which recovers at most +3 GT pairs on ONE repo (logrus) and +0 on cobra/gin while injecting net-new pairs of which a MEASURED 28pct are linked only by a same-named function-LOCAL variable in an unrelated file (param/root/engine/reset) — a static identifier walk cannot tell a package-var read from a same-named local without scope resolution tree-sitter does not provide, so the signal cannot be separated from a ~28pct false-coupling rate; for a precision-first product (quality IS precise silence) that is net-negative wallpaper, so the naive edge is NOT shipped. This gate LOCKS the boundary: (GAP) a deterministic Go fixture proves two sibling same-package files coupled only through a package-level const+var get ZERO edge today and the const/var mint no def node; (HAZARD) an unrelated file with a same-named LOCAL variable is NOT coupled to the const/var home file (a regression that naively fans const/var identifiers into edges is caught); (CONTROL) the same coupling expressed via a normal cross-package import IS captured, proving the miss is Go same-package symbol sharing specifically, not a dead extractor. Content-free (paths/symbol names/counts only), pure extractor, no DB, parallel-safe. Precision invariant (false_coupling) untouched." "go same-package const/var recall: the dominant measured Go co-change miss (sibling files sharing a package-level const/var with no import) is locked as a measured, not-safely-closable boundary — a precision lock that catches any regression naively fanning const/var identifiers into false couplings while documenting the real recall gap"
